### Which @angular/* package(s) are the source of the bug?

forms

### Is this a regression?

No

### Description

Please take a look at the following code:

<details>

```typescript
import { Component, OnInit, signal, model } from '@angular/core';
import { bootstrapApplication } from '@angular/platform-browser';
import { FormField, FormValueControl, form } from '@angular/forms/signals';

interface TestFormInterface {
  text: string;
}

@Component({
  selector: 'app-control',
  template: `
    <span>Current value {{ value() }}</span>
    <button (click)="updateValue()">Update value</button>
  `,
})
export class Control implements OnInit, FormValueControl<string> {
  public readonly value = model<string>("");

  ngOnInit(): void {
    this.value.subscribe((value) => {
      console.log(`Changed to ${value}`);
    })
  }

  protected updateValue(): void {
    this.value.set("Second");
  }
}

@Component({
  imports: [
    Control,
    FormField,
  ],
  selector: 'app-root',
  template: `
    <app-control [formField]="testForm.text" />
    <button (click)="updateForm()">Update form</button>
    <button (click)="log()">Log</button>
  `,
})
export class App {
  private readonly testFormModel = signal<TestFormInterface>({
    text : "First",
  });
  protected readonly testForm = form(this.testFormModel, (schemaPath) => {});

  protected updateForm(): void {
    this.testFormModel.set({
      text: "Third",
    });
  }

  protected log(): void {
    console.log(this.testFormModel());
  }
}

bootstrapApplication(App);
```
</details>

It implements a custom `FormValueControl` for Signal Forms which displays the value.

The example has 3 buttons:
- `Update value`: This is part of the control. It updates the value directly.
- `Update form`: Updates the value that is used in the control through the form.
- `Log`: This prints the value of the form on the console.

The custom control subscribes to the changes to the value and print every changes.

If you click `Update value` the value is changes and the `subscribe` callback is called.

If you click `Update form` the value is changes and the `subscribe` callback is **not** called.

So the value is changed in both, but updating the value through the form doesn't call the `subscribe` callback. This causes problems if you need to run custom code when the value changes.

